  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 12.0.1\n\n- Desktop apps can target .NET 8 or later. iOS, Android and WebAssembly apps need .NET 10.\n- Home and End jump to the first and last page. Cmd+Enter commits inline text editing on macOS and iOS.\n- Rotated shapes resize correctly.\n- Selecting an annotation no longer changes the colours and style of the next one you draw.\n- Text boxes without a fill no longer turn black while typing.\n- Fixed a crash after applying a redaction, and an error when closing a sticky note by placing a stamp.\n- The table of contents follows the current page, search shows its progress, and annotation tools stay disabled until a document is open.\n- Damaged or malicious PDFs are handled more safely: malformed files fail quickly instead of hanging, and link prompts cannot be spoofed.\n- Redaction also removes annotations and form values that were only reachable through references from other objects.\n- Updated to PDFium 157.",
